{"id":"gameliftservers","corpus":"aws","title":"Amazon GameLift Servers","sourceUrl":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/gameliftservers/latest/developerguide/gamelift-intro.html","license":"AWS Documentation © Amazon Web Services, Inc.","blocks":[{"kind":"h1","text":"Amazon GameLift Servers"},{"kind":"p","text":"Use Amazon GameLift Servers to deploy, operate, and scale dedicated, low-cost servers in the cloud for session-based multiplayer games. Built on AWS global computing infrastructure, Amazon GameLift Servers helps deliver high-performance, high-reliability game servers while dynamically scaling your resource usage to meet worldwide player demand."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Key features"},{"kind":"li","text":"Deploy hosting in AWS Regions and Local Zones worldwide to bring your games to new players. See a complete list of locations supported by Amazon GameLift Servers."},{"kind":"li","text":"Deliver lowest possible latency and great player experience, wherever your players are located."},{"kind":"li","text":"Use multi-location placement queues to dynamically place players into game sessions with optimal player experiences."},{"kind":"li","text":"Optimize fleet capacity for cost efficiency while maintaining quality of service."},{"kind":"li","text":"Scale capacity based on player demand using target-based auto scaling"},{"kind":"li","text":"Maintain capacity buffer to handle sudden player influxes."},{"kind":"p","text":"See more details at Amazon GameLift Servers game hosting options."},{"kind":"li","text":"Game hosting in the cloud, managed by Amazon GameLift Servers"},{"kind":"li","text":"Host game servers on Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2) infrastructure. Choose from resource types including compute-optimized (C-family), memory-optimized (R-family), and cost-efficient ARM-based Graviton instances."},{"kind":"li","text":"Customize how Amazon GameLift Servers manages all aspects of your game hosting solution, from deploying game servers and starting game sessions to matching players and getting them into games."},{"kind":"li","text":"Use multi-location fleets to streamline global game server deployment."},{"kind":"li","text":"Take advantage of low-cost hosting with Amazon EC2 Spot Instances."},{"kind":"li","text":"Deploy Windows or Linux game servers with managed EC2 hosting."},{"kind":"li","text":"Deploy Linux-based containers with your game server with managed container hosting."},{"kind":"li","text":"Game hosting managed by you, with Amazon GameLift Servers Anywhere"},{"kind":"li","text":"Leverage Amazon GameLift Servers game session placement and session management capabilities."},{"kind":"li","text":"Self-manage game server deployments and scaling on your own hardware, on-premises infrastructure, or other cloud providers."},{"kind":"li","text":"Hybrid game hosting"},{"kind":"li","text":"Create a game hosting solution that uses a combination of Amazon GameLift Servers managed fleets and Anywhere fleets to work with existing solutions or support migration."},{"kind":"li","text":"Let Amazon GameLift Servers manage game server processes for you, track game server status and availability, and place new game sessions on request."},{"kind":"li","text":"Use game session placement features to help players find and join game sessions that will provide the best possible player experience. Rely on Amazon GameLift Servers decision-making, or customize around criteria such as hosting cost, player latency, and geographic location."},{"kind":"li","text":"Create game session placement queues to efficiently process new game session requests. Use features to set a balance between placement quality and speed that fits your game and player expectations."},{"kind":"li","text":"Take advantage of optional player session features to reserve player slots in game sessions, validate players on connection, and monitor slot availability. Search or filter existing game sessions to find available slots."},{"kind":"li","text":"Add robust matchmaking that's fully integrated with your Amazon GameLift Servers hosting solution."},{"kind":"li","text":"Build custom matchmaking rules based on player attributes and preferences, such as skill level or character choice, and use complex logic as needed."},{"kind":"li","text":"Set up team-based matches for competitive or cooperative gameplay. Balance players across team and/or match composition."},{"kind":"li","text":"Optimize the matchmaking algorithm to balance match quality and wait times."},{"kind":"li","text":"Support matches from 2 to 200 concurrent players."},{"kind":"li","text":"Support match backfilling to fill available player slots and keep game sessions full."},{"kind":"li","text":"Get real-time metrics on usage and performance for game sessions and player activity, as well as hosting performance and health for managed fleets."},{"kind":"li","text":"Integrate with Amazon CloudWatch for alerts and dashboards."},{"kind":"li","text":"Access server logs and event tracking for troubleshooting."},{"kind":"li","text":"Analyze performance and utilization data to optimize scaling (managed fleets) or resource allocation (self-managed fleets)."},{"kind":"li","text":"Customize game session placement logic, including prioritizing for latency, cost, and location."},{"kind":"li","text":"For managed hosting, choose your game hosting resources and provide instructions for launching and running game servers on each instance. For managed containers, fine-tune resource allocation across containers."},{"kind":"li","text":"Define your own matchmaking rules."},{"kind":"li","text":"Implement custom strategies for capacity scaling."},{"kind":"li","text":"Add game server code to integrate with your existing AWS services, such as databases or content storage tools."},{"kind":"li","text":"Create a backend service with custom features to manage player join requests (such as player parties), handle authentication, or add custom logic and persistence."},{"kind":"li","text":"Use services such as Amazon DynamoDB, Amazon Simple Storage Service, and Amazon Aurora DSQL for game state persistence."}],"lemmas":{"amazons":["amazon","amazons"],"servers":["server","servers"],"used":["used","use"],"deploys":["deploys","deploy"],"deployed":["deployed","deploy"],"operates":["operates","operate"],"operated":["operated","operate"],"operating":["operating","operate"],"scales":["scale","scales"],"scaled":["scaled","scale"],"dedicated":["dedicated","dedicate"],"dedicateds":["dedicateds","dedicated"],"dedicates":["dedicates","dedicate"],"lows":["low","lows"],"lower":["lower","low"],"costs":["cost","costs"],"costing":["costing","cost"],"clouds":["cloud","clouds"],"clouding":["clouding","cloud"],"clouded":["clouded","cloud"],"based":["based","base"],"baseds":["baseds","based"],"bases":["base","bases"],"basing":["basing","base"],"multiplayers":["multiplayers","multiplayer"],"games":["game","games"],"gaming":["gaming","game"],"built":["built","build"],"builts":["builts","built"],"builds":["build","builds"],"building":["building","build"],"globals":["globals","global"],"computing":["computing","compute"],"computings":["computing","computings"],"computes":["computes","compute"],"computed":["computed","compute"],"infrastructures":["infrastructure","infrastructures"],"helps":["help","helps"],"helping":["helping","help"],"helped":["helped","help"],"delivers":["delivers","deliver"],"delivering":["delivering","deliver"],"delivered":["delivered","deliver"],"highs":["high","highs"],"higher":["higher","high"],"highest":["highest","high"],"performances":["performance","performances"],"reliabilities":["reliability","reliabilities"],"dynamicallies":["dynamicallies","dynamically"],"scaling":["scaling","scale"],"scalings":["scaling","scalings"],"usages":["usage","usages"],"meets":["meet","meets"],"meeting":["meeting","meet"],"met":["met","meet"],"worldwides":["worldwides","worldwide"],"demands":["demand","demands"],"demanded":["demanded","demand"],"demanding":["demanding","demand"],"keys"